caption.p:
The solid dots represent the experimental data (marked with “Exp”) reported in a recent study[35], while the hollow dots and those with “+” center are the ODEs and SSA results constructed from timestamp t = 1.0 × 105 in the time series (see Fig. S13), respectively. The plankton community data were obtained separately from the Norwegian Sea (NS) and Pacific Station (PS). In the model settings, SR = 1 (in (b, c)), 3 (in (a)); SC = 50 (in (a, c)), 150 (in (b)). Di (i = 1, …, SC) is the only parameter varying with the consumer species, which was randomly drawn from a Gaussian distribution. The Shannon entropies of the experimental data and simulation results for each plankton community are: 

